  "content": "Here is the step-by-step exact integer arithmetic solution.\n\n**Given values:**\n$a = 137$\n$b = 29$\n$c = 11$\n\n**Expression to compute:**\n$$ (a \\cdot b + c^3) - (a - b) \\cdot c $$\n\n### Step 1: Compute $a \\cdot b$\n$$ 137 \\cdot 29 $$\n\nBreakdown:\n$$ 137 \\cdot 29 = 137 \\cdot (30 - 1) = (137 \\cdot 30) - 137 $$\n$$ 137 \\cdot 30 = 4110 $$\n$$ 4110 - 137 = 3973 $$\n\nSo, **$a \\cdot b = 3973$**.\n\n### Step 2: Compute $c^3$\n$$ 11^3 = 11 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 11 $$\n$$ 11 \\cdot 11 = 121 $$\n$$ 121 \\cdot 11 = 1331 $$\n\nSo, **$c^3 = 1331$**.\n\n### Step 3: Compute the first parenthesis $(a \\cdot b + c^3)$\n$$ 3973 + 1331 $$\n\nCalculation:\n  3973\n+ 1331\n------\n  5304\n\nSo, **$(a \\cdot b + c^3) = 5304$**.\n\n### Step 4: Compute $(a - b)$\n$$ 137 - 29 $$\n\nCalculation:\n  137\n-  29\n-----\n  108\n\nSo, **$(a - b) = 108$**.\n\n### Step 5: Compute $(a - b) \\cdot c$\n$$ 108 \\cdot 11 $$\n\nCalculation:\n$$ 108 \\cdot 11 = 108 \\cdot (10 + 1) = 1080 + 108 = 1188 $$\n\nSo, **$(a - b) \\cdot c = 11",
